        "authorName": "xarantolus",
        "name": {
          "en-US": "Offline HN"
        },
        "summary": {
          "en-US": "Hacker News Client with offline caching of pages"
        },
        "description": {
          "en-US": "Offline HN is an unofficial <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com\">Hacker News</a> reader that downloads stories, comments and linked articles on Wi-Fi, so you can read them offline.\n\n<b>Features</b>\n\n- Top, Best, Ask and Show feeds with search\n- Collapsible comment threads\n- Saved copies of linked articles, with ads and cookie banners removed\n- Background updates, by default only on Wi-Fi and while charging\n- Swipe between feeds and stories, hide read stories\n\n<b>Limitations</b>\n\n- Read-only: no login, voting or commenting\n- Pages behind logins or captchas can't be saved, video links are skipped\n\nThe app connects to the Hacker News API, Algolia, the linked websites and filter list hosts, so it's labeled with \"NonFreeNet\".\n\nThis app is significantly vibe-coded / created using LLMs. Most of its code has not been thoroughly reviewed by a human.\n\nOffline HN is not affiliated with or endorsed by Y Combinator.\n"
        },
